{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":16382677,"ns":0,"title":"Armchair theorizing","extract":"Armchair theory or armchair philosophy is an approach to providing new developments in a field that does not involve analysis of empirical (real-world) data. The term is typically pejorative, implying such scholarship is weak, frivolous, and disconnected from reality.","description":"Analyzing existing work, without new data","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}